## 3. Level 2 — eight gated improvements (trigger → effect → rationale)

**L2-1. Early-Мишень weight.** After the weight-locals block (:557-577): `if (Smart(game) && game.RoundNo <= 4) isTargetTaretNumber = SmartTargetTaretNumberEarly;` (consumed at :666-671). *Мишень gains decay 10,9,…,1 and double-dip Main+Extra — an early capture is worth ~3× a late one, yet L1 weighs it +1 vs −5/−7 justice penalties.*

**L2-2. Known-class nemesis targeting (revives the dead info).** In the per-target loop after the nemesis block (:673-679). Bot legitimately owns `bot.Status.KnownPlayerClass` (written on nemesis losses `DoomsdayMachine.cs:39-53` / Мишень hits :566-590; currently read into a dead local at `CharacterPassives.cs:6298` and used by nothing):
```csharp
if (Smart(game))
{
    var knownTell = bot.Status.KnownPlayerClass.Find(x => x.EnemyId == target.GetPlayerId());
    if (knownTell != null)
    {
        var myType = bot.GameCharacter.GetSkillClassType();
        var counterKeyword   = CharacterClass.ClassToKnownKeyword(CharacterClass.NemesisOf(myType));
        var countersMeKeyword = CharacterClass.ClassToKnownKeyword(
            CharacterClass.NemesisOf(CharacterClass.NemesisOf(myType))); // 3-cycle: nemesis-of-nemesis counters me
        if (counterKeyword != "" && knownTell.Text.Contains(counterKeyword) && target.AttackPreference >= 5)
            target.AttackPreference += SmartKnownClassNemesisNumber;
        else if (countersMeKeyword != "" && knownTell.Text.Contains(countersMeKeyword))
            target.AttackPreference -= SmartKnownClassNemesisNumber;
    }
}
```
APIs verified: `ClassToKnownKeyword` `CharacterClass.cs:724`, `NemesisOf` :739, `GetSkillClassType` :756; `KnownPlayerClassClass{EnemyId, Text}` `InGameStatusClass.cs:389-399`. At implementation, sanity-check the keyword strings actually appear in the tell text (both are produced from the same mapping). *Nemesis = ±2 weighing + ×1.5 attacker skill term — the cheapest verified win-predictor available without cheating.*

**L2-3. Per-target justice gradient.** At :683-687, L1 rewards justice advantage only when **all** targets are below the bot. Add else-branch: `else if (Smart(game) && botJustice > targetJustice) target.AttackPreference += botJustice - targetJustice;` *Justice diff feeds the weighing term, Step-2 tiebreak and Step-3 window — per-target gradient is the correct generalization; negative side already exists at L1 (−5/−7).*

**L2-4. Fight-history horizon −3.** Extend the else-if chain at :629-646 with one more branch: same shape as the round−2 check but `x.RoundNo == game.RoundNo - 3 && x.IsStatsBetterEnemy`, reusing `isLostLastRoundAndTargetIsBetterNumber` **and setting the same `isLostLastRoundAndTargetIsBetter` flag**. *Stat-decided losses stay valid ≥3 rounds (stats only move on level-ups); reusing the exact flag/number keeps the mylorik (:988-998) and Глеб (:1149-1162) compensations balanced.*

**L2-5. Predicted-character avoidance (uses `bot.Predict` beyond the Братишка rule).** Immediately after :1755 (same per-target loop; loop closes :1757):
```csharp
if (Smart(game))
{
    var predictWeight = Omni(game) ? OmniPredictConfidence : 1;   // L3-1: predictions are certain
    var predicted = bot.Predict.Find(x => x.PlayerId == target.GetPlayerId());
    if (predicted != null)
    {
        // Краборак «Панцирь»: first attack per enemy = auto-block, +3 моральки +33 скилла ему
        if (predicted.CharacterName == "Краборак"
            && !bot.Status.WhoToLostEveryRound.Any(x => x.EnemyId == target.GetPlayerId())
            && !target.Player.Status.WhoToLostEveryRound.Any(x => x.EnemyId == bot.GetPlayerId()))
            target.AttackPreference -= SmartPredictAvoidNumber * predictWeight;

        // Толя «Раммус»: мораль = attackers² — don't join a pile on Толя
        if (predicted.CharacterName == "Толя"
            && allTargets.Any(x => x.Player.Status.WhoToAttackThisTurn.Contains(target.GetPlayerId())))
            target.AttackPreference -= SmartPredictAvoidNumber * predictWeight;
    }
}
```
*Both passives punish exactly this attack decision; weights small (−2, −4 at L3) since L2 predictions can be wrong. Note: Bot-mode games pre-fill true predictions (factory :96-106), so sims exercise this with perfect info even at L2 — acceptable, document it.*

**L2-6. Round-10 block economics.** After the Монстр place-1 force-block guard (:2435-2441), before `//mandatory attack` (:2446):
```csharp
if (Smart(game) && game.RoundNo == 10 && isBlock != noBlock && isBlock != yesBlock
    && minimumRandomNumberForBlock == 1 && maximumRandomNumberForBlock == 4)
{
    if (bot.Status.GetPlaceAtLeaderBoard() == 1) isBlock = yesBlock;   // defend the crown
    else isBlock = noBlock;                                            // ×4 round: justice is worthless now, attack
}
```
*Round 10 is ×4 regular points and the game ends before justice matters again. Leader: blocking denies challengers the +4/Harm swing and taxes each attacker −1 bonus. Everyone else: blocking earns nothing that still matters. The untouched-generic guard (`min==1 && max==4`, `isBlock` not forced) preserves every character's bespoke round-10 logic (Сайтама :2004-2011, Спартанец :2171-2188, Школьник :2121-2124, Монстр :2344-2349 + game guard :2436-2441).*

**L2-7. Moral→points hoard thresholds.** `HandleBotMoralForPoints` :211/:214 — replace the two literals with gated ternaries, structure preserved: place 4 waits `Smart ? 13 : 8`, place 3 waits `Smart ? 8 : 5`. *Conversion tiers are strictly better higher (5→1, 8→2, 13→5, 20→10 = 0.20→0.50 pts/moral); conversions are bonus points (never ×2/×4) and the round-10 force-dump (`CheckIfReady.cs:1332-1335`) guarantees hoarded moral still cashes. Places 5-6 already hoard 13/20; places 1-2 need score now. Do NOT touch `HandleBotMoralForSkill` (skill curve nearly flat; early skill compounds — early spend is correct there).*

**L2-8. Zero-justice defensive block bias.** Same guarded region as L2-6, rounds 2-9: if `Smart && botJustice == 0` and generic block state untouched and `allTargets.All(x => x.AttackPreference < 6)` → `minimumRandomNumberForBlock = 2;` *At 0 justice you lose every tiebreak and are milked by Умный attackers; if no target scored ≥6 the heuristics found no good fight — raising the roll floor 1→2 nudges toward block (+1 next-round justice, −1 bonus tax per attacker) within the existing skeleton.*

*(Assessed & dropped: crowd/leader-pile logic — `howManyAttackingTheSameTarget` :660-662 only sees already-committed players, and the engine doesn't penalize piling except Толя/Еврей — Толя covered by L2-5.)*

